{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788353120102,"sessionID":"ses_f9dddfb2dffempxJY12lUiiE44","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ffa876ba692d47a79f8b358a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Pinned pyasc v2 limitations relevant to CANNBench\n2: \n3: This is a routing summary. Detailed evidence and confidence labels live in\n4: `docs/pyasc-v2-cannbench-blockers.md`.\n5: \n6: - Generated AscendC can declare the same scalar identifier for f16 and bf16,\n7:   producing a `c0_f16` redefinition. Isolate the half types or bridge through a\n8:   separate f32 buffer.\n9: - Direct arithmetic/cast paths from int8 tiles are incomplete. The observed\n10:   conversion route is int8 -> f16 -> f32.\n11: - Tile DMA requires a 32-byte-aligned final dimension even when `real_shape`\n12:   is smaller. Choose an aligned physical tile and a valid layout/fallback.\n13: - Static UB usage is sensitive to live SSA values and loop unrolling. Run the\n14:   exact compile gate for every specialization; keep a smaller-tile fallback.\n15: - Python-float loop accumulators cannot be reassigned to pyasc PlainValue/Tile\n16:   results. Seed with a reduction result of an aligned zero tile.\n17: - `asc2.where` requires tensor-valued branches, and tensor-only unary ops such\n18:   as `asc2.rsqrt` reject PlainValue reductions. Select scalar-compatible\n19:   algebra or explicitly materialize one aligned local tensor.\n20: - Local QEMU compilation cannot establish NPU runtime behavior, numerical\n21:   correctness, or performance.\n\n(End of file - total 21 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Pinned pyasc v2 limitations relevant to CANNBench\n\nThis is a routing summary. Detailed evidence and confidence labels live in\n`docs/pyasc-v2-cannbench-blockers.md`.\n\n- Generated AscendC can declare the same scalar identifier for f16 and bf16,\n  producing a `c0_f16` redefinition. Isolate the half types or bridge through a\n  separate f32 buffer.\n- Direct arithmetic/cast paths from int8 tiles are incomplete. The observed\n  conversion route is int8 -> f16 -> f32.\n- Tile DMA requires a 32-byte-aligned final dimension even when `real_shape`\n  is smaller. Choose an aligned physical tile and a valid layout/fallback.\n- Static UB usage is sensitive to live SSA values and loop unrolling. Run the\n  exact compile gate for every specialization; keep a smaller-tile fallback.\n- Python-float loop accumulators cannot be reassigned to pyasc PlainValue/Tile\n  results. Seed with a reduction result of an aligned zero tile.\n- `asc2.where` requires tensor-valued branches, and tensor-only unary ops such\n  as `asc2.rsqrt` reject PlainValue reductions. Select scalar-compatible\n  algebra or explicitly materialize one aligned local tensor.\n- Local QEMU compilation cannot establish NPU runtime behavior, numerical","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md","text":"# Pinned pyasc v2 limitations relevant to CANNBench\n\nThis is a routing summary. Detailed evidence and confidence labels live in\n`docs/pyasc-v2-cannbench-blockers.md`.\n\n- Generated AscendC can declare the same scalar identifier for f16 and bf16,\n  producing a `c0_f16` redefinition. Isolate the half types or bridge through a\n  separate f32 buffer.\n- Direct arithmetic/cast paths from int8 tiles are incomplete. The observed\n  conversion route is int8 -> f16 -> f32.\n- Tile DMA requires a 32-byte-aligned final dimension even when `real_shape`\n  is smaller. Choose an aligned physical tile and a valid layout/fallback.\n- Static UB usage is sensitive to live SSA values and loop unrolling. Run the\n  exact compile gate for every specialization; keep a smaller-tile fallback.\n- Python-float loop accumulators cannot be reassigned to pyasc PlainValue/Tile\n  results. Seed with a reduction result of an aligned zero tile.\n- `asc2.where` requires tensor-valued branches, and tensor-only unary ops such\n  as `asc2.rsqrt` reject PlainValue reductions. Select scalar-compatible\n  algebra or explicitly materialize one aligned local tensor.\n- Local QEMU compilation cannot establish NPU runtime behavior, numerical\n  correctness, or performance.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":21,"totalLines":21,"truncated":false}},"title":"skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md","time":{"start":1788353120092,"end":1788353120101}},"id":"prt_0622703f5001AQLeDttjwwOegx","sessionID":"ses_f9dddfb2dffempxJY12lUiiE44","messageID":"msg_06226db9c001Xvs7Q1d6xeUksF"}}
